-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Atic Atac
  Publisher   Ultimate
  Version     1.6

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Atic Atac (1983)(Ultimate Play The Game)[a8][a8].z80
  MD5         06b11e63d60401666332a61626a5789c

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The knight, wizard and serf, and most monsters, in fuller colour
              with more detail; the knight gets a red hat and green tunic. A
              few monsters turn a duller brown. Source: enhanced colours from
              an older Spec256 conversion (the MVV package), painter not
              established.

  Pace        original (+0.26% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless on the
              NextZXOS v2.09 card, against the plain build of the same start
              state; pass probe 0x7E44; R fixed per site at 9 sites, FRAMES at
              its logic reads and the player group's decision from a table, in
              both games; game state, 90 addresses, equal at every pass)

  Changes     1.1: faster hooks (an image cache, row lookups), no picture
              change. 1.2: door and furniture cells no longer flash red next
              to moving figures; the menu's screen clear no longer leaves the
              icons on screen. 1.3: option QAOP + Space keys (Q A O P to move,
              Space to fire, Caps Shift pauses). 1.4: original pace, never
              faster (limiter). 1.5: works on NextZXOS v2.10 (System/Next
              26.11). 1.6: the game now holds the original's pace; 1.5 lost 5
              to 10 frames at each room change and when monsters appeared.

  Note        With QAOP + Space on, Space fires, so only Caps Shift pauses.
              Plays at the original's pace in JNext, 2026-11-08, same input
              and game state equal at every pass, default and Enhanced, 4
              runs: overall -0.2 to +0.5%, quiet -0.2 to +0.5%, busy -0.2 to
              +0.8% (1.5, same measure: overall +2.0 to +3.8%, busy up to
              +4.6%). These rest on a test fixture in both games, as they do
              not stay in step as shipped; the earlier +0.83% and +14.5% were
              not like for like. Known issues: slowest stretch of 20 passes
              +1.7% in 600 passes, +4.0% in 1,500 (1.5: +18.6%, +31.2%), +2.6%
              with QAOP + Space on; fastest -5.8%, around first room entries
              and first monsters; enemies differ from run to run on the same
              keys (the game's chance comes from R, which the hooks change);
              the game reads a few ROM bytes as data and gets the Next ROM's
              values (effect on play not established). Missing: few rooms
              walked by script; hardware untested.

