  Coverage    v1.6: one more game-bank site, 0x9159 (the CALL that queues the
              room's sound); the sound routines' first bytes 0xA3AA and 0xA46E
              are swapped only while catch-up is on; pattern store and palette
              bytes as 1.5. Same target, loading screen, default and Enhanced
              pattern bytes, trainers and credit as v1.0/v1.1. v1.1 hook-speed
              engine plus: the figure painter's nine LD (HL),E vacated-cell
              writes are NOPs (as its LD (HL),D writes already were), and the
              whole-screen clear 0x80B4 is hooked. Original game logic, sound
              and delays byte-exact; the only changed game-bank bytes are
              those ten sites. v1.4: the same game-bank bytes as v1.3; the
              hook code adds the pace limiter (figure setups, text, scenery,
              room line and character setup hooks) and hook RAM 0x5BA9-0x5BAF.

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
